## Part 6: Technical Deep-Dive — Why This Works

### Why QUIC Eliminates the Black Screen

**HLS (current Sling) at an ad break:**
1. Current TCP segment must fully download
2. TCP connection to content CDN tears down
3. New TCP connection to ad CDN (3-way handshake: 50–200ms per hop)
4. Ad segment downloads at bitrate (~1–5 seconds)
5. Buffer fills before playback (~500ms minimum)

**Result: 1.5–7 seconds of guaranteed black screen**

**MOQ/QUIC at an ad break:**
1. Player sends `UNSUBSCRIBE(content-track)` — 1 round trip (~20ms at edge)
2. Player sends `SUBSCRIBE(ad-track)` — 1 round trip (~20ms at edge)
3. Relay forwards ad Objects immediately — first frame arrives ~40ms later
4. Player renders — no buffering (MOQ objects are frame-aligned)

**Result: 40–300ms — no black screen, ever**

Key insight: **QUIC is multiplexed.** The content and ad streams share the same connection simultaneously. A track switch is one protocol message, not a TCP reconnect.

---

### Why x402 Is Better Than Invoice-Based Ad Payment

| Dimension | Traditional CTV Payment | x402 Per-Impression |
|-----------|------------------------|-------------------|
| Settlement | 30–90 days | <2 seconds |
| Receipt | PDF invoice | Blockchain transaction |
| Fraud risk | High (no delivery proof) | None (payment requires delivery) |
| Minimum unit | ~$0.01 (card fees) | $0.0001 (Base L2 gas <$0.00001) |
| Programmatic | Semi-manual DSP billing | Fully autonomous (AI-agent compatible) |
| Disputes | Months, lawyers | Smart contract arbiter, instant |

---

### Why Base L2 (Not Ethereum Mainnet)

| Metric | Ethereum Mainnet | Base L2 |
|--------|-----------------|---------|
| Gas per tx | $2–15 | $0.0001 |
| Block time | 12 seconds | 2 seconds |
| TPS | ~15 | ~2,000 |

At $0.0001 USDC per impression, Ethereum mainnet gas would be **100x the payment value**. Base L2 is the only chain where per-impression unit economics are viable today.

---

## Part 7: Honest Disclosure of Phase 0 Limitations

> [!NOTE]
> Phase 0 is a working prototype — not a production system. All limitations below have explicit Phase 1 upgrade paths built into the codebase.

| Limitation | Current Reality | Phase 1 Path |
|-----------|----------------|-------------|
| **No Caton C3 SDK** | Using open-source `moq-rs` reference relay | One-line swap to `CatonC3Transport` — interface already implemented |
| **Ad auction is a stub** | Hardcoded winner, ~50ms simulated latency | Real DSP integration (Google Ad Manager, Magnite, etc.) |
| **SLA oracle is a trusted signer** | `DeliveryOracle.sol` uses our own ECDSA key | Upgrade to Chainlink CRE for decentralized verification |
| **Testnet only** | Base Sepolia — no real money | Phase 2: Base mainnet deployment |
| **Single node** | One EC2 instance | Phase 1: Raspberry Pi 5 deployment kit for EchoStar towers |
| **Healthcheck shows "unhealthy"** | Docker TCP probe fails on QUIC/UDP service | Cosmetic — relay is fully operational; fix uses QUIC-aware probe |
| **x402 uses test wallet** | Demo wallet, no real advertiser onboarding | Production: Coinbase Smart Wallet SDK for self-service advertiser UX |

